// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1219.002
// Description: An adversary may use legitimate desktop support and remote access software, such as Team Viewer,
//   Go2Assist, LogMein, AmmyyAdmin, etc, to establish an interactive command and control channel to
//   target systems within networks. These services are commonly used as legitimate technical support
//   software, and may be allowed by application control within a target environment. Remote access
//   tools like VNC, Ammyy, and Teamviewer are used frequently when compared with other legitimate
//   software commonly used by adversaries. (Citation: Symantec Living off the Land)
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1219/T1219.md#atomic-test-5---screenconnect-application-download-and-install-on-windows
